  "scaleNote": "This is a 250 m Terra MODIS NDVI point sample in the Banaue area of Ifugao, averaged from good- or marginal-reliability 16-day observations by month. It is a mixed mountain landscape sample, not a mapped rice paddy, terrace-condition survey, or harvest/yield measurement. UNESCO identifies five inscribed terrace clusters across four municipalities; the sample point is not a boundary or inventory of those clusters. NDVI measures vegetation greenness and cannot explain changes by itself. UNESCO conservation milestones provide cultural context, not proof of cause for a satellite reading. Months without accepted retrievals remain gaps; only interior gaps of up to two months are estimated for chart and audio.",
